  "term": "vestibular system",
  "definition": "The vestibular system is the set of inner-ear structures, eye-related components, parts of the central nervous system, and the nerves and pathways linking them that help the body sense position and maintain spatial orientation. Problems in this system are linked with disorders such as vertigo and motion sickness.",
